> This is not just GLM. It on MiMo-V2-Pro as well as MiniMax M2.7. Its not a model issue its an OpenCode bug

I've had same issue on MiMo-V2-Pro on the very first try, I've added frequency penalty to opencode.json to see if that can help :
```
  "provider": {
    "openrouter": {
      "models": {
        "xiaomi/mimo-v2-pro": {
          "options": {
            "frequency_penalty": 0.3
          }
        }
      }
    }
  }
```

EDIT: I spent a few hours doing work with the model, the issue was never observed. So it's either working or it's a coincidence.

PR #18539 Follow-up: _noop tool handling during LiteLLM compaction
PR #18539 addressed the issue where the _noop stub tool injected for LiteLLM/Bedrock compatibility was being called by the model during compaction, causing empty summaries and context loss (#14368, #18053). The fix relied on prompt-level discouragement ("Do not call any tools" in the compaction prompt) and updating the tool description to "Do not call this tool. It exists only for API compatibility and must never be invoked."
This is a soft constraint with no guarantee the model will comply.
A more robust fix is to set toolChoice: "none" at the API level for the compaction agent, which is a hard constraint that prevents the model from making any tool calls regardless of prompt wording. The _noop stub is still injected to satisfy LiteLLM's non-empty tools requirement, but the model is structurally blocked from invoking it.
// llm.ts
let compactionToolChoice: "none" | undefined
if (isLiteLLMProxy && Object.keys(tools).length === 0 && hasToolCalls(input.messages)) {
  tools["_noop"] = tool({
    description:
      "Placeholder for LiteLLM/Anthropic proxy compatibility - required when message history contains tool calls but no active tools are needed",
    inputSchema: jsonSchema({ type: "object", properties: {} }),
    execute: async () => ({ output: "", title: "", metadata: {} }),
  })
  if (input.agent.name === "compaction") {
    compactionToolChoice = "none"
  }
}
// then passed to streamText:
streamText({
  // ...
  toolChoice: compactionToolChoice ?? input.toolChoice,
})
This makes the prompt-level "Do not call any tools" line from PR #18539 unnecessary — toolChoice: "none" enforces it at the API level.
